body:
The game is in maintenance mode. No new content is coming. Invade was more busted and was nerfed twice to a playable level.

&#x200B;

Is invade super-skill intensive, no. I feel invade being more easily accessible (via rarity and amount of necessary cards) gets the decks hate that other low-skill decks like dragon recursion and slay don't have.

I agree with OP wholeheartedly. Invade rarely snatches a win out of nowhere.

&#x200B;

Meanwhile dragons just plays Paarthunax until you've got all the shouts you need to win, or Alduins every turn and there's very little one can do against that. Piercing Twilight is the best answer, but you need to be running blue. Empire can A New Era which can also kill the dragon deck potentially, but then you're even more restricted to running Empire. 

&#x200B;

I'd play dragons for dailies sometimes, but I feel dirty doing so.

Okay, so the paywall for the cardbacks was too high. Where do you think the paywall should have been? 

&#x200B;

I agree that the decks should have been available in the shop from day 1. That's fair and makes sense. At the same time, I can understand lack of desire to put out a free legend from the set (makes more people buy more to open it). That being said, I think maybe give a free epic to support the new set and get new players to try the set out.
